# Upwork Toolkit — Chrome Extension Walkthrough

## What Changed

The entire Node.js CLI scraper project has been **replaced** with a Chrome Manifest V3 extension as specified in the toolkit design document.

### Removed
- `index.mjs`, `search.mjs`, `enricher.mjs`, `scorer.mjs`, `config.mjs`
- `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `node_modules/`, `chrome_session/`, `.env`

### Created

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/manifest.json) | MV3 manifest with permissions for storage, notifications, alarms, scripting |
| [background.js](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/background.js) | Service worker — job polling via alarms, deduplication, notifications |
| [content.js](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/content.js) | Content script — proposal auto-fill, feed highlighting, DOM scraping |
| [content-styles.css](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/content-styles.css) | Injected CSS for highlighted/dimmed job cards |
| [popup.html](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/popup.html) / [popup.css](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/popup.css) / [popup.js](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/popup.js) | Popup UI with quick toggles |
| [options.html](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/options.html) / [options.css](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/options.css) / [options.js](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/options.js) | Full settings page with sidebar navigation |
| [README.md](file:///c:/Users/gurno/Desktop/Upwork/upwork-agent/README.md) | Documentation |

