## How to Install

1. Open Chrome → `chrome://extensions`
2. Enable **Developer Mode** (top-right toggle)
3. Click **Load Unpacked** → select `c:\Users\gurno\Desktop\Upwork\upwork-agent`
4. The extension icon appears in your toolbar

## Features Implemented

- ✅ **Job Alerts** — Alarm-based polling with Chrome notifications
- ✅ **Proposal Auto-Fill** — Template-based cover letter injection on proposal pages
- ✅ **Feed Highlighting** — Keyword/budget-based visual job card styling
- ✅ **Search Profiles** — CRUD with per-profile filters (keywords, budget, client rating)
- ✅ **Proposal Templates** — Multiple templates with tags, default selection
- ✅ **Feed Filters** — Keyword + minimum budget rules
- ✅ **Settings** — Polling interval, export/import, full reset
- ✅ **Badge Counter** — Unseen job count on the extension icon

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Background Worker<br/>(background.js)"] -->|chrome.alarms| B["Job Polling"]
    B -->|chrome.tabs.sendMessage| C["Content Script<br/>(content.js)"]
    B -->|fallback fetch| D["Direct HTML Parse"]
    A -->|chrome.notifications| E["Desktop Alerts"]
    C -->|DOM Injection| F["Proposal Auto-Fill"]
    C -->|CSS Classes| G["Feed Highlighting"]
    H["Popup<br/>(popup.js)"] -->|chrome.runtime.sendMessage| A
    I["Options Page<br/>(options.js)"] -->|chrome.storage.sync| A
```
